articles=[('article-seo.html','A Practical Starting Point for SEO','SEO','Search visibility is built through many small, connected decisions. Begin with a clear understanding of what your audience is looking for and how your site helps them.','Start with search intent','List the questions your customers ask before they choose a product or service. Group related questions and map them to useful pages rather than creating a separate page for every phrase.','Make the page useful','Use a specific page title, a clear main heading, concise explanations, and helpful next steps. Add internal links that help readers continue their journey.','Check the technical basics','Make sure important pages can be reached, load comfortably on mobile, and use descriptive links. Review indexing and performance data with an appropriate analytics setup.','Treat SEO as ongoing learning','Compare relevant queries and pages over time. Keep useful content current and use evidence to decide what to improve next. This sample editorial article is pending agency review.'),('article-social.html','Plan Social Content with Purpose','Social media','A useful social plan gives a business a repeatable way to share its perspective without turning every week into a scramble.','Choose a few content themes','Themes can reflect customer questions, product knowledge, behind-the-scenes work, or the people and values behind a brand. Keep them connected to what the business actually offers.','Match formats to the idea','Short video, carousels, photos, and text posts each do different jobs. Choose formats your team can create consistently and your audience can use.','Build a realistic rhythm','Plan around available time and resources. A calendar should make publishing easier, while leaving room for timely conversations and learning.','Review and refine','Look at saves, replies, clicks, and other relevant signals in context. Use the patterns to inform the next cycle rather than chasing every trend. This sample editorial article is pending agency review.'),('article-landing.html','Make Your Landing Page Clearer','Website development','A landing page works best when a visitor can quickly understand what is being offered, who it is for, and what to do next.','Lead with the value','Use a clear headline and supporting description that explain the offer in familiar language. Keep one primary action easy to find.','Answer useful questions','Explain what is included, who benefits, and what happens after a visitor reaches out. Use real details and avoid unsupported claims.','Reduce friction','Make the layout easy to scan, ensure forms ask only for relevant information, and test the experience on a phone.','Learn from real behavior','Use a privacy-conscious analytics setup to understand where visitors engage or pause. Treat improvements as hypotheses to review. This sample editorial article is pending agency review.')]
